01:01:04.430 --> 01:01:05.530
She used to go out to the store

01:01:05.530 --> 01:01:07.090
and then come back five minutes later

01:01:07.090 --> 01:01:09.270
and forget why she went out.

01:01:09.270 --> 01:01:12.590
- I don't remember that.

01:01:12.590 --> 01:01:16.450
- Remember the time you forgot your birthday?

01:01:16.450 --> 01:01:18.630
- In front of Tommy.

01:01:18.630 --> 01:01:20.570
I didn't forget my own birthday.

01:01:20.570 --> 01:01:24.650
I just got the days a little bit mixed up.

01:01:24.650 --> 01:01:28.100
I didn't, and I was only one day off.

01:01:28.100 --> 01:01:29.760
- Hi, Brenda, you about ready?

01:01:31.210 --> 01:01:32.840
- Two o'clock already?

01:01:32.840 --> 01:01:36.560
I almost drank all time.

01:01:36.560 --> 01:01:41.720
Ross, this is Tommy, this is Jason, this is Ross.

01:01:41.720 --> 01:01:44.690
- Hi, nice to meet you.

01:02:07.260 --> 01:02:08.690
Can you go please?

01:02:08.690 --> 01:02:10.740
Come on baby, I'm just getting warmed up.

01:02:10.740 --> 01:02:11.740
Just getting warmed up?

01:02:11.740 --> 01:02:12.740
You've been there a half hour?

01:02:12.740 --> 01:02:13.740
Can we please go?

01:02:13.740 --> 01:02:14.850
I'm ready.

01:02:14.850 --> 01:02:15.850
Look, five minutes, okay?

01:02:15.850 --> 01:02:16.850
Just give me five more minutes.

01:02:16.850 --> 01:02:18.850
Five minutes and then we leave.

01:02:18.850 --> 01:02:20.610
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:02:20.610 --> 01:02:22.200
Yeah.

01:02:22.200 --> 01:02:29.070
Taken.

01:02:30.120 --> 01:02:31.120
So keep moving.

01:02:31.120 --> 01:02:35.720
I don't smoke.

01:02:35.720 --> 01:02:37.850
You got your time?

01:02:37.850 --> 01:02:38.800
Yeah.

01:02:38.800 --> 01:02:40.800
It's about time I kicked your ass in.

01:02:40.800 --> 01:02:46.710
Jennifer?

01:02:46.710 --> 01:02:50.640
Jennifer, I don't believe you are here.

01:02:50.640 --> 01:02:52.460
I'm laying low for a few days, alright?

01:02:52.460 --> 01:02:53.460
So just be cool.

01:02:53.460 --> 01:02:55.350
I've been so worried about you, Jennifer.

01:02:55.350 --> 01:02:58.620
I'm really sorry to hear about your mom.

01:03:00.440 --> 01:03:01.420
I'm so sorry.

01:03:01.420 --> 01:03:02.780
Crazy times.

01:03:06.370 --> 01:03:07.780
So where are you staying?

01:03:07.780 --> 01:03:09.280
I lucked out, I met some great people.

01:03:09.280 --> 01:03:10.440
That's so good, Jennifer.

01:03:10.440 --> 01:03:12.620
I've been so worried about you.

01:03:12.620 --> 01:03:13.780
Listen, where's Elsa at?

01:03:13.780 --> 01:03:15.340
I've been trying to reach both of you all week.

01:03:15.340 --> 01:03:19.500
She's been staying with us since, you know.

01:03:19.500 --> 01:03:20.960
She's feeling it too, you know?

01:03:20.960 --> 01:03:22.510
Look, I gotta talk to her right away.

01:03:22.510 --> 01:03:23.650
Okay, we'll go now.

01:03:23.650 --> 01:03:25.270
Yo, yo, what the fuck?

01:03:25.270 --> 01:03:27.530
Yo, that's my girl, yo, what the fuck is going on here?

01:03:27.530 --> 01:03:28.770
Larry, wait.

01:03:31.880 --> 01:03:44.250
- Jennifer?

01:03:44.250 --> 01:03:46.030
- Nothing, last week I really could have been

01:03:46.030 --> 01:03:48.650
the domestic violence poster girl.

01:03:48.650 --> 01:03:50.590
- Gotta report this guy, Elsa.

01:03:50.590 --> 01:03:52.800
- No, not an option in this case.

01:03:52.800 --> 01:03:55.420
- Go ahead, it'll be all right.

01:03:55.420 --> 01:03:58.160
- What?

01:03:58.160 --> 01:03:59.030
- Jennifer, I...

01:04:01.660 --> 01:04:03.680
She thinks that what happened is her fault.

01:04:03.680 --> 01:04:04.660
It's not.

01:04:04.660 --> 01:04:06.160
Don't put yourself through this.

01:04:06.160 --> 01:04:08.160
Why couldn't I just be with Frank?

01:04:08.160 --> 01:04:10.160
I mean, I loved him so much.

01:04:10.160 --> 01:04:13.520
Would somebody please clue me in here?

01:04:15.590 --> 01:04:17.410
The men who came to your house,

01:04:17.410 --> 01:04:19.760
they were looking for drugs.

01:04:19.760 --> 01:04:23.760
Drugs that I stole and gave to Frank.

01:04:23.760 --> 01:04:25.600
I'm sorry.

01:04:25.600 --> 01:04:26.600
Calm down, honey.

01:04:26.600 --> 01:04:28.480
Forgive me, Jennifer.

01:04:30.570 --> 01:04:42.240
Calm down honey. It's not your fault. You're not responsible for this. You're not.

01:04:51.970 --> 01:04:56.670
So how are you doing?

01:04:57.200 --> 01:04:58.580
I'm hanging in there.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.740
Listen, I don't want Elsa to know this, but I got the stuff.

01:05:02.740 --> 01:05:04.590
Well, how the hell did that happen?

01:05:04.590 --> 01:05:07.160
My dear stepfather didn't exactly hand it to me.

01:05:07.160 --> 01:05:10.470
Damn, this is fucked up.

01:05:10.470 --> 01:05:12.180
Yeah, and I gotta fix it.

01:05:12.180 --> 01:05:13.860
I gotta unload the stuff and get the money for it.

01:05:13.860 --> 01:05:16.390
Can you help me with that?

01:05:16.390 --> 01:05:18.580
Probably.

01:05:18.580 --> 01:05:23.740
I'm working tonight, so I'll ask around.

01:05:23.740 --> 01:05:28.780
Samples.

01:05:28.780 --> 01:05:30.000
This has to happen fast.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:36.120
people after me let me know you cut and where are you gonna go they say the

01:05:36.120 --> 01:05:40.460
beaches of Portugal can't be beat you sure you have to do something that

01:05:40.460 --> 01:05:58.000
drastic I'm sure what can I do for you tonight

01:06:00.410 --> 01:06:01.830
The lady in my hand, give me my usual.

01:06:02.460 --> 01:06:04.000
Margarita, salt, no ice.

01:06:05.850 --> 01:06:07.600
Hey, come here.

01:06:08.360 --> 01:06:08.800
Yeah, boss.

01:06:09.390 --> 01:06:10.020
Did you call Carlos?

01:06:10.260 --> 01:06:11.560
Yeah, boss, I just got off the phone with him.

01:06:11.680 --> 01:06:13.420
He said the earliest for that shipment is next week.

01:06:13.920 --> 01:06:14.660
I need it tonight.

01:06:15.450 --> 01:06:17.410
Boss, he keeps telling me the earliest is next week.

01:06:17.450 --> 01:06:18.170
I don't know what to tell you.

01:06:18.530 --> 01:06:19.330
I need it tonight.

01:06:19.810 --> 01:06:20.570
Go give him a call.

01:06:20.710 --> 01:06:21.490
Tell him what I told you.

01:06:21.510 --> 01:06:23.070
You know I gotta go pick it up myself tonight, okay?

01:06:23.490 --> 01:06:23.770
Okay.

01:06:25.030 --> 01:06:26.430
Cheers.

01:06:29.680 --> 01:06:30.000
Dimitri.

01:06:31.120 --> 01:06:33.200
I, uh, came across something.

01:06:33.200 --> 01:06:36.600
What you're most familiar with.

01:06:36.600 --> 01:06:38.780
I didn't know you were interested in the subject.

01:06:38.780 --> 01:06:42.840
Although, it was my capability to...

01:06:42.840 --> 01:06:44.890
Well, this is a one-time thing.

01:06:44.890 --> 01:06:47.180
It just kind of presented itself.

01:06:47.180 --> 01:06:50.540
Alright. You know who I am.

01:06:50.540 --> 01:06:53.810
You know where to find me if you need anything.

01:06:53.810 --> 01:06:56.370
Congratulations, sir.

01:06:56.370 --> 01:06:58.420
Cheers.

01:07:01.440 --> 01:07:03.840
Sure was a good meal Maggie cooked for us, I'm full.

01:07:03.840 --> 01:07:06.180
It's a good woman who knows how to cook.

01:07:06.180 --> 01:07:09.220
Oh, borrowing lines from Jennifer now, are we?

01:07:09.220 --> 01:07:12.820
Uh-huh. She knows a lot about life. I like her.

01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:16.550
Sweet girl.

01:07:16.550 --> 01:07:19.280
Pretty, too.

01:07:19.280 --> 01:07:23.280
Come on, let's have a seat.

01:07:23.280 --> 01:07:29.120
How come seagulls never fly into the city and pigeons don't fly to the beach?

01:07:30.600 --> 01:07:36.930
has something to do with their instincts. A pigeon would look funny on the beach. Yeah.

01:07:36.930 --> 01:07:45.020
Would you like to swim in the ocean? Not really. I can, but I can't see the bottom. I might

01:07:45.020 --> 01:07:52.120
step on something. Like a fish or a crab or something? Like garbage. Was the ocean polluted

01:07:52.120 --> 01:08:00.000
when you were a kid? No. Not like it is now. See how old your old man is. I want to swim

01:08:00.060 --> 01:08:06.690
study that when I'm older. It's called, um, some kind of biology.

01:08:06.690 --> 01:08:10.260
Marine biology? Right. I want to become a marine biologist.

01:08:10.260 --> 01:08:16.370
That's terrific. If you're serious about that, California's the place you should be.

01:08:16.370 --> 01:08:19.010
Your mom could help. No thanks.

01:08:19.010 --> 01:08:22.330
You know, Brenda called me this morning. She and Ross are going back to L.A. and they've

01:08:22.330 --> 01:08:26.320
invited you for a week. I'm not moving there.

01:08:26.320 --> 01:08:30.000
Just for a week. Just to see how you like it. You want to get

01:08:30.000 --> 01:09:00.000
rid of me again? That's not true. Then why are you saying this? Tommy, I'm just trying to figure out what's best for you in the long run. She's a stranger to me. And Ross, who the hell is he? Tommy, they can give you the things that I can't. Good schools, a stable home. They've got horses on their property for God's sake. If I were you, I'd want to live there. If you don't want me around, just say so. I'll go back to Aunt Maggie's. Tommy, I had to have you.

01:09:01.790 --> 01:09:02.790
I know how you feel.

01:09:02.790 --> 01:09:06.490
No one's gonna take you away from me, you got that?

01:09:06.490 --> 01:09:12.640
Let's just forget we ever had this conversation.

01:09:12.640 --> 01:09:13.950
Except for one thing.

01:09:13.950 --> 01:09:16.050
I love you, Tom.

01:09:16.050 --> 01:09:18.410
I love you too, dude.

01:09:18.410 --> 01:09:24.720
So how long do you know this guy?

01:09:24.720 --> 01:09:27.730
He's worked over at Wrigley's for about three years.

01:09:27.730 --> 01:09:29.570
He's always been helpful.

01:09:41.960 --> 01:09:43.440
Trust me boss, it's good stuff.

01:09:43.440 --> 01:09:46.610
I have to check it out before we agree on anything.

01:09:46.610 --> 01:09:48.780
He wants to make this deal as soon as possible.

01:09:48.780 --> 01:09:50.590
Don't they always?

01:09:50.590 --> 01:09:51.700
Call me tonight.

01:09:51.700 --> 01:09:53.170
Okay boss, will do.

01:10:06.720 --> 01:10:12.420
Hey, it's me. I think I find what you are looking for. We'll know it tonight.

01:10:12.420 --> 01:10:17.670
Before we get into Tommy, I really want to apologize for the other day.

01:10:17.670 --> 01:10:22.350
I didn't mean for things to go that way. I thought that by the time Ross came in...

01:10:22.350 --> 01:10:28.240
Look, I realize that. I realize that, but what pisses me off is that you're still trying to manipulate things to your own advantage.

01:10:28.240 --> 01:10:30.000
That's not going to blow the chance of meeting my own son.

01:10:30.700 --> 01:10:35.040
I wouldn't have, you know, I don't know whether you overestimate me or underestimate me.

01:10:35.040 --> 01:10:36.250
Both.

01:10:36.250 --> 01:10:37.200
Well, at least you admit it.

01:10:37.200 --> 01:10:39.450
I'm absolutely horrible, aren't I?

01:10:39.450 --> 01:10:42.930
You're not a pain in the ass, as usual.

01:10:42.930 --> 01:10:45.580
Brenda, look, I didn't come here to make enemies.

01:10:45.580 --> 01:10:49.870
As a matter of fact, we have to be friends, for Tommy's sake.

01:10:49.870 --> 01:10:52.520
If I have you for a friend, it would be for my own sake, as well.

01:10:52.520 --> 01:10:54.030
Look, I talked to Tommy.

01:10:54.030 --> 01:10:56.320
He wants to stay with me.

01:10:56.320 --> 01:10:58.400
Now, he came to that decision on his own.

01:10:58.400 --> 01:10:59.830
That doesn't surprise me.

01:11:00.540 --> 01:11:02.610
- Does he ever want to see me again?

01:11:02.610 --> 01:11:04.840
- Yeah, but I don't think he knows that yet.

01:11:04.840 --> 01:11:06.440
I want him to spend a couple of days with you

01:11:06.440 --> 01:11:08.040
before you go back.

01:11:08.040 --> 01:11:09.240
- Would he?

01:11:09.240 --> 01:11:12.950
Oh, Jason, if that could happen.

01:11:12.950 --> 01:11:16.830
- Tell you what, I'll bring him over

01:11:16.830 --> 01:11:18.750
so he can spend some time with you and Ross,

01:11:18.750 --> 01:11:20.910
but if he wants to come back at any time.

01:11:20.910 --> 01:11:23.510
- Of course, I don't want to push him.

01:11:23.510 --> 01:11:26.240
You don't know how thrilled I am.

01:11:26.240 --> 01:11:28.020
- Actually, I do.

01:11:28.020 --> 01:11:30.000
I felt the same way about a week ago.

01:11:41.160 --> 01:11:48.060
your Aunt Nancy. Hi, Tommy. Are you really a cop? Yes, I am. That's really cool. Thank

01:11:48.060 --> 01:11:57.460
you. Thanks for bringing him early. No problem. Every minute really counts. Hey, Tommy, what

01:11:57.460 --> 01:11:59.960
do you want to do to me, kid? I don't really care.

01:12:00.250 --> 01:12:02.210
We were thinking about the Museum of Natural History.

01:12:02.210 --> 01:12:08.160
Yeah, as a kid I was crazy about dinosaurs, brontosaurs, tyrannosaurs.

01:12:08.160 --> 01:12:10.850
The largest herb ever is dinosaur.

01:12:10.850 --> 01:12:13.320
Brontosaurs are my favorite.

01:12:13.320 --> 01:12:14.660
The museum it is then.

01:12:14.660 --> 01:12:16.010
Are you coming?

01:12:16.010 --> 01:12:18.530
I can't. I have to go back to work.

01:12:18.530 --> 01:12:20.070
But I have off tomorrow.

01:12:20.070 --> 01:12:22.240
How would you like to go rollerblading in Central Park?

01:12:22.240 --> 01:12:23.930
Well, I don't have rollerblades.

01:12:23.930 --> 01:12:25.960
Hey, you know what? We'll get you a pair today.

01:12:25.960 --> 01:12:27.170
Oh, thanks.

01:12:27.170 --> 01:12:30.000
Ben!

01:12:32.400 --> 01:12:34.110
- Hi. - Hey.

01:12:34.110 --> 01:12:35.610
- This is my partner, David.

01:12:35.610 --> 01:12:37.190
David, this is my sister, Brenda.

01:12:37.190 --> 01:12:38.230
- Hey, Brenda, nice to meet you.

01:12:38.230 --> 01:12:39.180
- How you doing?

01:12:39.180 --> 01:12:40.420
- And this is her husband, Ross.

01:12:40.420 --> 01:12:41.980
- Hey, Ross, nice to meet you.

01:12:41.980 --> 01:12:43.440
- This is my nephew, Tommy.

01:12:43.440 --> 01:12:45.190
- Tommy, how are you, man?

01:12:45.190 --> 01:12:49.930
- And his father, Jason.

01:12:49.930 --> 01:12:52.420
- Well, I'm sorry to cut this short, but I gotta go.

01:12:52.420 --> 01:12:53.260
- Okay.

01:12:53.260 --> 01:12:54.110
- It's nice meeting you.

01:12:54.110 --> 01:12:54.990
- I'll see you tomorrow.

01:12:54.990 --> 01:12:58.940
Okay, and Brenda, I'll call you later.

01:12:58.940 --> 01:12:59.380
Bye.

01:13:01.630 --> 01:13:05.760
All right son, have a good time, okay buddy?

01:13:05.760 --> 01:13:06.900
- See you dad.

01:13:06.900 --> 01:13:09.470
- Couple days now.

01:13:09.470 --> 01:13:10.440
- What do you wanna do for dinner?

01:13:44.680 --> 01:13:49.930
Dear Jason, if all goes according to my plan, there will soon be enough money for your share of the coffee house.

01:13:50.430 --> 01:13:51.110
Good luck with it.

01:13:52.020 --> 01:13:54.940
By the time you read this, I will have sold the drugs and bought a one-way ticket out of here.

01:13:55.280 --> 01:14:00.000
Tell Victor thank you and tell Tommy he's the most incredible person I have ever met.

01:14:00.990 --> 01:14:02.030
That is besides you.

01:14:03.190 --> 01:14:04.390
Love always, Jennifer.

01:14:04.790 --> 01:14:05.090
Victor!

01:14:07.490 --> 01:14:08.510
Check this out, man.

01:14:09.480 --> 01:14:11.080
She's gonna sell the drugs and leave town.

01:14:11.160 --> 01:14:12.800
Did she say where she's gonna go, or?

01:14:13.240 --> 01:14:16.180
No, she was on the phone, then I got into the shower,

01:14:16.260 --> 01:14:18.000
and by the time I got out, she was gone.

01:14:19.430 --> 01:14:24.640
What the hell are you doing?

01:14:25.260 --> 01:14:29.190
What the hell is that?

01:14:30.030 --> 01:14:31.610
- This is not far from here, man.

01:14:31.610 --> 01:14:32.810
- No, you don't know how to do that.

01:14:32.810 --> 01:14:34.610
- You can't, come on.

01:15:00.030 --> 01:15:01.210
I'll see you again, man.

01:15:01.210 --> 01:15:02.210
You ready to do business?

01:15:02.210 --> 01:15:03.210
Of course.

01:15:03.210 --> 01:15:04.210
Let's see what you can have.

01:15:04.210 --> 01:15:06.160
Take a look for yourself.

01:15:06.160 --> 01:15:26.400
Do you have my money?

01:15:30.440 --> 01:15:31.940
- Sure.

01:15:31.940 --> 01:15:32.990
- Here it is.

01:15:38.230 --> 01:15:39.810
Nice.

01:15:39.810 --> 01:15:41.630
You gonna count it?

01:15:41.630 --> 01:15:44.670
- Nah, I trust you.

01:15:44.670 --> 01:15:46.080
- It's a dangerous business.

01:15:46.080 --> 01:15:48.260
Friends are your enemies, the enemies are your friends.

01:15:48.260 --> 01:15:49.460
- I don't need to know all that, man.

01:15:49.460 --> 01:15:52.810
I'm just in and out.

01:15:52.810 --> 01:15:55.810
- Not like the thrill of your first deal, is that?

01:15:55.810 --> 01:15:58.280
- First and last, man.

01:15:58.280 --> 01:15:59.320
- Be careful.

01:16:31.660 --> 01:16:33.650
Come on.

01:18:36.040 --> 01:18:45.930
I was right man, so I promise I'm going to get you to a hospital.

01:18:48.340 --> 01:18:52.150
You're the best friend I've ever had man.

01:18:52.150 --> 01:18:53.860
I'm going to make it.

01:18:53.860 --> 01:18:55.290
I want you to do something for me.

01:18:55.290 --> 01:18:56.530
Sure.

01:18:56.530 --> 01:18:59.360
I want you to get out of here before the cops come.

01:18:59.360 --> 01:19:00.000
No way.

01:19:00.160 --> 01:19:11.080
No way, I'm so sorry for leaving, I'm so sorry.

01:19:49.070 --> 01:19:50.630
How's Paulette?

01:19:50.630 --> 01:19:51.630
She finally fell asleep.

01:19:51.630 --> 01:19:57.440
All I ever wanted to do was do the right thing.

01:19:57.440 --> 01:19:58.450
I know.

01:20:02.880 --> 01:20:07.840
Wait, wait. You think I went through all this just to have you leave now?

01:20:09.140 --> 01:20:14.450
About love? You cared for my son?

01:20:14.720 --> 01:20:18.880
I need you. I want you to be a part of our family.

01:20:19.940 --> 01:20:21.300
Please don't leave.

01:21:33.000 --> 01:21:35.550
Hi, Dad, it's Tommy.

01:21:37.010 --> 01:21:38.710
Well, I'm at Central Park right now.

01:21:39.100 --> 01:21:40.440
You wouldn't believe it, but I'm blading.

01:21:41.180 --> 01:21:43.760
Well, we just got to the boat park,

01:21:43.890 --> 01:21:45.410
and now we're about to have lunch.

01:21:45.590 --> 01:21:46.810
I'm glad you're having a good time.

01:21:46.870 --> 01:21:47.910
Be careful on those skates.

01:21:48.340 --> 01:21:49.660
I mean, blades.

01:21:50.000 --> 01:21:52.000
Be careful on those blades, okay?

01:21:52.440 --> 01:21:53.630
I'll see you later. Bye.

01:21:53.850 --> 01:21:54.890
Okay, see you, Dad.

01:22:02.300 --> 01:22:03.990
- Tommy.

01:22:03.990 --> 01:22:06.810
- Yeah, he's at Central Park, he's having a great time.

01:22:06.810 --> 01:22:08.490
- Jason, I'm worried.

01:22:08.490 --> 01:22:11.020
You better go get him.

01:22:11.020 --> 01:22:12.420
- What is it?

01:22:12.420 --> 01:22:13.780
- I talked to Elsa.

01:22:13.780 --> 01:22:15.660
- When?

01:22:15.660 --> 01:22:17.130
- A few days ago.

01:22:17.130 --> 01:22:18.490
She's staying with Paulette.

01:22:19.300 --> 01:22:20.420
I didn't tell you because I thought

01:22:20.420 --> 01:22:23.960
I was taking care of everything.

01:22:23.960 --> 01:22:25.200
Frank got the drugs from her

01:22:25.200 --> 01:22:28.650
and she got them from this cop that she was seeing.

01:22:28.650 --> 01:22:29.540
- A crooked cop?

01:22:30.160 --> 01:22:32.830
- Oh, they're the worst.

01:22:32.830 --> 01:22:36.190
Okay, we gotta take care of this mess right away.

01:22:36.190 --> 01:22:37.430
I mean, this cop knows everything,

01:22:37.430 --> 01:22:39.620
so I want you to call Elsa

01:22:39.620 --> 01:22:46.100
and set up a meeting with him as soon as you can.

01:22:46.100 --> 01:22:48.640
- Hey, guys.

01:22:48.640 --> 01:22:49.970
- Hi, I'm late.

01:22:49.970 --> 01:22:51.290
- Hey, where's your rollerblades?

01:22:51.290 --> 01:22:52.800
- I had some police business this morning,

01:22:52.800 --> 01:22:54.720
so I didn't have time to get 'em.

01:22:54.720 --> 01:22:56.360
- The life of a police officer, I guess, huh?

01:22:56.360 --> 01:22:59.710
- No, but you skate, I'll jog.

01:22:59.710 --> 01:23:00.000
- Okay.

01:23:00.380 --> 01:23:01.220
- I'll take pictures.

01:23:01.220 --> 01:23:03.940
- Okay. - Okay, good.

01:23:03.940 --> 01:23:16.990
- I usually run here every morning before I go to work.

01:23:16.990 --> 01:23:18.310
- Tell me where the men's room is.

01:23:18.310 --> 01:23:20.150
- Uh, yeah, you see that building right there?

01:23:20.150 --> 01:23:26.520
You just go off to the left.

01:23:26.520 --> 01:23:27.410
- What's up?

01:23:27.410 --> 01:23:28.320
I got 'em, I got 'em.

01:24:07.900 --> 01:24:10.860
It's not taking them too long.

01:24:10.860 --> 01:24:11.460
There they are.

01:25:00.760 --> 01:25:01.600
- You okay?

01:25:01.600 --> 01:25:02.340
- Yeah, yeah.

01:25:02.340 --> 01:25:04.540
- Hey!

01:25:04.540 --> 01:25:07.950
- Ah!

01:25:07.950 --> 01:25:12.560
- On duty, detective vouch, 72nd precinct.

01:25:12.560 --> 01:25:13.660
- Why'd they kidnap Tommy?

01:25:13.660 --> 01:25:15.680
You wanna tell me what this is about?

01:25:15.680 --> 01:25:17.360
- You wanna ask your partner, David,

01:25:17.360 --> 01:25:19.450
the crooked cop who's dealing drugs?

01:25:19.450 --> 01:25:27.530
- What?

01:25:27.530 --> 01:25:28.550
- Hello, Elsa.

01:25:28.550 --> 01:25:29.380
Missed you.

01:25:30.860 --> 01:25:33.710
Well, when you were good, I took real good care of you.

01:25:34.090 --> 01:25:35.670
You only took care of yourself.

